.TH UAC 4 "June 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
uac \- USB Audio Class playback driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <drivers/usb/usb.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B uac
driver binds USB Audio Class (UAC) functions and exposes their playback
path through the
.BR audio (4)
framework as a
.B /dev/audioN
device, so the ordinary audio stack \(em
.BR mpg123 ,
.BR /dev/audio
writers, the
.B audioio
ioctls \(em drives a USB headset or DAC.
.PP
The driver supports playback (host-to-device) only; capture endpoints are
ignored.  It handles both UAC 1.0 and UAC 2.0 functions that present a
single sample clock and a 16-bit alternate setting.
.SS Operation
When an audio function is enumerated, the driver:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Walks the configuration descriptor for the AudioStreaming interface's
playback alternate setting, preferring a 16-bit format (matching the
framework's signed-16 path), and locates its isochronous OUT endpoint and
.IR wMaxPacketSize .
.IP 2. 4
Locates the clock entity feeding the USB-streaming input terminal and,
for UAC 2.0, sets it to 48 kHz with a clock-source
.B SET_CUR
request.
.IP 3. 4
Issues
.B SET_INTERFACE
to activate the alternate setting, bringing the isochronous endpoint
live.
.IP 4. 4
Registers an
.BR audio (4)
device whose
.BR write (2)
streams PCM straight to the endpoint.
.RE
.SS Isochronous Transfer
Audio is carried over an isochronous OUT endpoint: one packet per 1 ms
frame at full speed, no handshake and no retry.  The
.B uhci
host controller driver schedules one transfer descriptor per frame
directly into the frame list, a couple of frames ahead of the
controller, and streams large buffers in bounded batches.  A
.BR write (2)
of
.I n
bytes blocks for roughly
.IR n / wMaxPacketSize
milliseconds while the controller emits the buffer.
.SS Format
The device is presented to userland as 48 kHz, signed 16-bit
little-endian, stereo.  Because a UAC device commonly runs a fixed
clock, the playback rate is driven at 48 kHz regardless of the requested
rate; feed 48 kHz S16 stereo PCM for correct pitch.
.SH HARDWARE
The driver matches any device whose interface class is
.B USB_CLASS_AUDIO
with an AudioControl interface, independent of UAC protocol version.  It
has been developed against the Apple EarPods
.RB ( 05ac:110b ),
a full-speed UAC 2.0 headset whose playback path is interface 1,
alternate setting 2 (16-bit/48 kHz/stereo) on isochronous OUT endpoint
.BR 0x02 .
.SH NOTES
Only full-speed isochronous OUT is implemented; isochronous IN
(capture), feedback endpoints, and explicit sample-rate conversion are
not.  A source that is not 48 kHz is played without resampling.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dev/audioN
The audio sample device registered for the bound function.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR audio (4),
.BR write (2)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B uac
driver and the UHCI isochronous transfer path it depends on were added
together to bring USB audio playback to Substrate.
